across the capitol  across the nation  silence  a moment to reflect for the people  and their new king  [Applause]  he was issued this statement on the eve  of his mother's funeral  as we all prepared to say our last  farewell he said i wanted simply to take  this opportunity to say thank you to all  those countless people who've been such  a support and comfort to my family  and myself and this time of grief  the happy more extraordinary scenes in  westminster hall  ordinary mourners joined by a stream of  foreign dignitaries  the kings of spain and  sweden the first lady of ukraine clearly  moved and presidents from around the  world  u.s president joe biden joining mourners  to pay his respects  she was the same in person as her image  decent honorable  and all about service it's a loss that  leaves a giant hole  and uh  sometimes you think you'll never  you'll never overcome it but  as i've told the king  she's going to be with him every step of  the way every minute every moment  and that's a reassuring notion  one of a hundred heads of governments  gathering here from emperors to crown  princes there are 20 royals among 500  foreign guests  the prime minister of that team  they know this will never be repeated  because a unique era is drawing to a  close  another beginning not least for the  commonwealth whose leaders met king  charles earlier today  on the eve of the funeral a prediction  from the president of trinidad and  tobago that under the new king more and  more commonwealth countries will give up  the monarch as head of state as the  times continue changing  there is a feeling now after all these  years that the sovereign should really  be the people  and that to have a sovereign from a  country that is far removed  not only geographically but culturally  right might not necessarily be the best  thing at this time of the nation's  development  so i think that perhaps the process will  begin speeding up  in various territories  what would be your emotions  what will be going through your  your mind as you sit in the abbey  tomorrow looking back on the era  i thought well i really would have to  carry my handkerchief with me because  it's quite possible  that i may shed a tear  for the queen  at this funeral death will be the great  leveler whatever the rank dignitaries  all arriving in coach class bust in from  chelsea's royal hospital  being corralled in a glorified holding  pen and then put on buses is not what  world leaders are used to but it is the  only option say officials who've never  had to deal with so many foreign  dignitaries all at the same time  barters leaders and dignitaries filed  into buckingham palace this evening a  sense of the enormity of this occasion  the world's most influential and  powerful people gathering together to  pay a final tribute  to a monarch loved like no other  dominic waghorn sky news westminster

